WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.850
- That's a weird question.

00:00:00.850 --> 00:00:03.420
- Oh, this is a too weird question.

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:04.580
- Is this a trick question?

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:06.860
- Damn, where the hell'd you
come up with this question?

00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:08.320
- Can I ask you a question about it?

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:09.153
- [Thoraya] Yeah, sure.

00:00:09.153 --> 00:00:12.463
- Is that assuming that
it's missing within me?

00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:14.860
- [Thoraya] However
you wanna interpret it?

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:16.753
- Oh.
- [Thoraya] It's up to you.

00:00:16.753 --> 00:00:21.753
- I miss most about myself,
even though I do it every day,

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:25.524
is smiling and laughing.

00:00:25.524 --> 00:00:28.300
I always love how that feels.

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:33.300
I realized it when I went
through a bad breakup.

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:36.420
And towards the end of the relationship

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:39.957
I realized I wasn't smiling a lot.

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:44.040
And when I went through the breakup,

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:46.400
certain things started to uplift me

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:50.270
as I get more into myself,
and learned myself,

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:52.060
and learned to love myself again.

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:55.610
And I started to realize at some point

00:00:55.610 --> 00:01:00.250
my cheeks hurt, like I'm smiling a lot.

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:03.910
And I used to feel so shy
about it at the beginning,

00:01:03.910 --> 00:01:06.880
I was like, oh, am I, why
am I the only one smiling?

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:09.180
Am I the only one feeling like this?

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:12.650
And I realized it didn't
matter if I was or wasn't,

00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:14.260
because even I was,

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:17.420
if someone else could feel
it they'll feel like it too.

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:22.200
So, it just felt good
to feel and go through.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:25.960
But I went through a
period of not feeling it

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:30.270
for a long time before I realized that.

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:33.706
So, I guess I had to be
without appreciate it more.

00:01:33.706 --> 00:01:36.910
(gentle music)

00:01:36.910 --> 00:01:39.593
- I miss being so naive and innocent.

00:01:40.490 --> 00:01:42.550
I miss thinking like a child.

00:01:42.550 --> 00:01:45.630
I have so much knowledge
now about the world,

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:47.560
that I just miss being like,

00:01:47.560 --> 00:01:51.100
like innocent and stupid, not
know nothing about the world.

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:54.063
'Cause it's a really harsh
world that we live in today.

00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:56.460
- I miss the way I was

00:01:56.460 --> 00:02:01.030
before I knew that depression overtook me

00:02:01.030 --> 00:02:06.030
and before I started like
purposely hurting myself,

00:02:06.570 --> 00:02:09.620
because I thought that things were normal

00:02:09.620 --> 00:02:12.930
and I felt happier and more innocent.

00:02:12.930 --> 00:02:15.190
I dunno, I think it
was slightly over time,

00:02:15.190 --> 00:02:18.110
but I did have like a few triggers,

00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:21.950
like getting bullied and just like,

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:24.490
I also have struggled
with an eating disorder

00:02:24.490 --> 00:02:27.620
and that just like
really degraded my brain

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:29.750
and the way that I thought of things.

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:34.063
And I feel like one day I just
gave up on life completely.

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:37.907
- Probably when I was little

00:02:37.907 --> 00:02:42.473
and I wouldn't care what others
would think, like about me.

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:45.230
But like, as we get older,

00:02:45.230 --> 00:02:50.230
we realize what the standards
that society puts for one.

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:54.170
Well, I've always been like a bigger kid.

00:02:54.170 --> 00:02:55.210
And when I was little,

00:02:55.210 --> 00:02:58.900
I wouldn't care when
people would like call me,

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:00.940
you know, big, fat, whatever,

00:03:00.940 --> 00:03:03.420
'cause I would just like let it slide.

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:04.890
But, when we get older,

00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:08.633
we kind of realize like
the meaning behind that.

00:03:10.090 --> 00:03:11.260
Yeah.

00:03:11.260 --> 00:03:12.930
(gentle music)

00:03:12.930 --> 00:03:16.870
- So, I'm slowly starting to
get this part of myself back,

00:03:16.870 --> 00:03:19.300
but I miss being happy.

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:21.410
I was very unhappy for a long time

00:03:22.270 --> 00:03:24.640
dealing with a lot of disrespect

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:26.790
in the relationship that I was in.

00:03:26.790 --> 00:03:29.577
And I finally left that and it's,

00:03:29.577 --> 00:03:31.750
I'm learning to be myself again.

00:03:31.750 --> 00:03:32.910
Which is a whole new self

00:03:32.910 --> 00:03:35.193
because I was with this
person for 11 years.

00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:39.090
So, it's been a learning process

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:42.230
and I'm honestly enjoying
getting to know myself

00:03:42.230 --> 00:03:47.230
'cause I'm learning I'm
really awesome. (laughing)

00:03:47.570 --> 00:03:51.250
And I don't know, it's, I'm
learning to be happy again.

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:55.937
And that's something that's
really, really important

00:03:55.937 --> 00:03:59.790
because, I don't know, I
wasn't happy for a long time,

00:03:59.790 --> 00:04:02.140
so I'm really happy that
I'm getting that back.

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:05.683
- I miss knowing myself.

00:04:06.790 --> 00:04:11.123
So, I was also in a ten year relationship.

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:14.720
And you do become one.

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:17.190
And so I was, I was interested in things,

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:21.050
and watching things, and reading
things, and eating things

00:04:21.050 --> 00:04:25.773
that I realized like
weren't even my choices.

00:04:28.150 --> 00:04:30.180
So, in the last few months I'm learning

00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:32.040
what do I actually like?

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:34.870
Who am I? What do I enjoy?

00:04:34.870 --> 00:04:37.000
Figured out that I like
eating an early dinner,

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:39.563
but something I haven't done in 10 years.

00:04:39.563 --> 00:04:41.740
I really like, like a five o'clock dinner,

00:04:41.740 --> 00:04:43.080
but I was used to a 10 o'clock.

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:45.230
So, that's nice.

00:04:45.230 --> 00:04:50.090
I like traveling with my
friends only. (laughing)

00:04:50.090 --> 00:04:51.480
Yeah. So I, I miss myself,

00:04:51.480 --> 00:04:55.850
because I feel like I gave up on myself.

00:04:55.850 --> 00:04:57.580
- [Thoraya] Was it like an
ah-ha moment? (indistinct)

00:04:57.580 --> 00:04:58.430
- Yeah, actually,

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:01.120
when I discovered that
I like early dinners.

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:02.956
And I know that sounds so silly

00:05:02.956 --> 00:05:05.503
and like such a weird thing to say,

00:05:07.210 --> 00:05:12.000
but once I started living without him

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:14.010
I started paying attention to myself.

00:05:14.010 --> 00:05:16.090
Like actually paying attention
to me. What do I want?

00:05:16.090 --> 00:05:18.220
And I'm like, oh, I'm, I'm hungry.

00:05:18.220 --> 00:05:19.960
It's 5:00 PM. It's still daylight.

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:22.070
I'm hungry. I made myself dinner.

00:05:22.070 --> 00:05:24.830
I sat down and I ate it,
and I was so satisfied.

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:29.830
And then it hit me like I
haven't done this in years

00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:32.020
and I cried.

00:05:32.020 --> 00:05:33.210
You know, that sounds so silly.

00:05:33.210 --> 00:05:35.870
but I cried at the fact that I
got to eat dinner at 5:00 PM,

00:05:35.870 --> 00:05:37.576
when I was hungry.

00:05:37.576 --> 00:05:40.653
And I wasn't concerned about
anybody else. I was hungry.

00:05:41.730 --> 00:05:45.583
- Uh, I miss when I
was more compassionate.

00:05:46.940 --> 00:05:49.770
When I was younger, I
was very, very caring

00:05:49.770 --> 00:05:51.763
and very trusting, trusting person.

00:05:51.763 --> 00:05:53.510
Then I got near some people

00:05:53.510 --> 00:05:55.430
who wasn't really, really, for me.

00:05:55.430 --> 00:05:58.175
They would only be cool when
it was convenient for them.

00:05:58.175 --> 00:06:00.770
And I thought making myself more reserved

00:06:00.770 --> 00:06:03.950
would solve that problem,
but I still feel the same.

00:06:03.950 --> 00:06:06.530
Ever since I had my
daughter, I've softened up

00:06:06.530 --> 00:06:10.750
and I've like learned
to let people more in

00:06:10.750 --> 00:06:13.776
than I would like to, but it's a process.

00:06:13.776 --> 00:06:16.359
(gentle music)

00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:28.230
- I think I miss the confidence
I had when I was younger.

00:06:28.230 --> 00:06:30.570
- I miss the confidence
that I used to have.

00:06:30.570 --> 00:06:32.500
- I miss my confidence.

00:06:32.500 --> 00:06:34.550
- [Thoraya] What made you lose that?

00:06:34.550 --> 00:06:36.143
- Trauma. The world.

00:06:37.610 --> 00:06:42.610
I guess I lost my ability to be confident

00:06:43.020 --> 00:06:47.070
because of how other
people are in the world,

00:06:47.070 --> 00:06:48.683
their judgments, their,

00:06:53.616 --> 00:06:55.699
the harm that they cause.

00:06:56.670 --> 00:07:00.070
- So, I have clinical
depression, and I have anxiety,

00:07:00.070 --> 00:07:04.190
and I have cyclothymia,
which is a bipolar disorder.

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:08.360
And I miss feeling okay.

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:10.480
I, you know, I was talking
about it with a friend

00:07:10.480 --> 00:07:12.100
and sometimes I wake up

00:07:12.100 --> 00:07:13.800
and I'm like I don't, I
don't wanna do anything.

00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:15.790
Like, I don't want to get out of bed.

00:07:15.790 --> 00:07:18.150
I miss feeling like myself,

00:07:18.150 --> 00:07:20.760
'cause I used to be this
like very bubbly person.

00:07:20.760 --> 00:07:21.630
And right now I feel like

00:07:21.630 --> 00:07:23.420
I'm just like faking it till I make it.

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:24.840
Which, you know,

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:28.030
it's probably not the
best coping mechanism,

00:07:28.030 --> 00:07:29.270
but I do go to therapy

00:07:29.270 --> 00:07:31.670
and I go with my psychiatrist every month.

00:07:31.670 --> 00:07:34.780
And so I miss feeling okay

00:07:34.780 --> 00:07:38.333
and feeling comfortable
with being vulnerable.

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:41.680
- I would say my depression,

00:07:41.680 --> 00:07:43.570
whenever, you know, at a young age

00:07:43.570 --> 00:07:46.280
trauma and all that good stuff happens.

00:07:46.280 --> 00:07:48.780
And then when you get
around to finally fixing it

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:50.300
you don't really realize who you are.

00:07:50.300 --> 00:07:52.450
So, it's fun learning about yourself,

00:07:52.450 --> 00:07:53.950
but I gotta say, I do miss it.

00:07:55.750 --> 00:07:57.780
My favorite spice blend that I made

00:07:57.780 --> 00:08:02.350
was one that I made while
in a bad mental breakdown.

00:08:02.350 --> 00:08:04.060
And I, I kinda miss that

00:08:04.060 --> 00:08:05.780
'cause that means I won't be able to make

00:08:05.780 --> 00:08:08.422
that type of a spice
blend again. (laughing)

00:08:08.422 --> 00:08:12.071
That was a weird answer. But, yeah.

00:08:12.071 --> 00:08:14.863
- [Thoraya] So, you
miss having depression?

00:08:16.520 --> 00:08:18.350
- Being motivated to do things

00:08:18.350 --> 00:08:21.023
that other people want me to do.

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:24.450
I used to kind of thrive

00:08:24.450 --> 00:08:27.610
on the thought of people being proud of me

00:08:27.610 --> 00:08:30.033
for doing things like school.

00:08:32.030 --> 00:08:36.330
But I, it's, it's not really
that I don't care anymore,

00:08:36.330 --> 00:08:39.000
it's just like, like
I, I feel so burnt out

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:40.253
that that doesn't really,

00:08:41.380 --> 00:08:44.280
that's not something that
strikes me as important anymore.

00:08:45.340 --> 00:08:46.263
Yeah. That's it.

00:08:47.099 --> 00:08:49.810
- I think I miss the excitement

00:08:49.810 --> 00:08:52.653
of getting up in the morning for game day.

00:08:54.130 --> 00:08:56.630
I've been a basketball my entire life,

00:08:56.630 --> 00:09:01.120
and that's always kind
of been my identity.

00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:05.480
And it wasn't until probably high school

00:09:05.480 --> 00:09:08.410
that I fell out of love with the game.

00:09:08.410 --> 00:09:09.810
Something that I really miss

00:09:11.170 --> 00:09:12.003
is just

00:09:15.310 --> 00:09:18.250
being excited to play a game

00:09:19.130 --> 00:09:23.740
that I love without any pressure,
without any expectation.

00:09:23.740 --> 00:09:25.600
Being from where I'm from,

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:26.830
there's not a lot of kids

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:30.370
that get out of my situation
from where I grew up.

00:09:30.370 --> 00:09:34.170
And so I felt like I
always had a responsibility

00:09:34.170 --> 00:09:38.120
to play basketball, earn a scholarship,

00:09:38.120 --> 00:09:42.473
go to school, and make
something of myself.

00:09:42.473 --> 00:09:47.473
- I think I miss being able
to fight things head on.

00:09:49.040 --> 00:09:51.560
I think I got a little bit too soft.

00:09:51.560 --> 00:09:55.710
I used to be real strong in
the way I advocated for myself.

00:09:55.710 --> 00:09:59.150
And now I'm a little bit too forgiving.

00:09:59.150 --> 00:10:01.000
- [Thoraya] What made you lose that?

00:10:02.980 --> 00:10:04.913
- Wanting certain people in my life.

00:10:09.300 --> 00:10:14.300
- I think that it is sort
of restoring my faith.

00:10:17.330 --> 00:10:20.230
I think I lost sight of it. I
don't know if I'm losing it.

00:10:22.710 --> 00:10:25.210
Yeah, I mean, I dunno how
to describe it, I guess.

00:10:26.060 --> 00:10:29.630
And, you know, like the component

00:10:29.630 --> 00:10:32.100
of just not feeling guilty.

00:10:32.100 --> 00:10:35.363
I think that's, to me, yeah.

00:10:36.510 --> 00:10:38.693
Yeah, it's like I get it,

00:10:39.770 --> 00:10:44.770
but I think I can reach
the same levels of goodness

00:10:45.980 --> 00:10:50.980
by not being held
accountable to that extent.

00:10:51.360 --> 00:10:52.193
You know what I mean?

00:10:52.193 --> 00:10:53.620
Like I know it was
getting really technical,

00:10:53.620 --> 00:10:57.130
but religion, I guess,
is the way I see that.

00:10:57.130 --> 00:11:01.900
But, yeah, I think overall is
just continue to explore it.

00:11:01.900 --> 00:11:04.460
You know, like thinking
about getting back to it,

00:11:04.460 --> 00:11:07.430
just like continue to explore it

00:11:07.430 --> 00:11:10.783
until you get some sort of concise answer.

00:11:11.950 --> 00:11:12.783
- Hm.

00:11:15.010 --> 00:11:18.800
Having my, all my brains. Doing things.

00:11:18.800 --> 00:11:21.730
I can't do stuff anymore
now. I'm 66 years old.

00:11:21.730 --> 00:11:25.450
I can't do anything, so that bothers me.

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:27.930
But when I was young, I was a spitfire.

00:11:27.930 --> 00:11:31.053
I skydived, I rock climbed, I repelled,

00:11:33.162 --> 00:11:34.852
I rode the rapids,

00:11:34.852 --> 00:11:36.833
I've been in the ocean, I flew a plane.

00:11:38.020 --> 00:11:41.340
I've been in the Army.
I can't do 'em anymore.

00:11:41.340 --> 00:11:43.713
I can't do none of those things.

00:11:46.930 --> 00:11:49.650
My memory's not good right now anymore.

00:11:49.650 --> 00:11:51.300
See, it's a lot of things.

00:11:51.300 --> 00:11:53.070
I'm a mess, but I'm fighting it all.

00:11:53.070 --> 00:11:56.403
So, I'm not too happy to, you
know, to die anytime soon.

00:11:57.838 --> 00:12:02.163
But when it comes, I'm ready. Yeah.

00:12:03.082 --> 00:12:04.513
- [Thoraya] Well, thank you
for answering my questions.

00:12:04.513 --> 00:12:05.346
- You're welcome hon.

00:12:05.346 --> 00:12:06.179
- [Narrator] I appreciate you.

00:12:06.179 --> 00:12:07.020
- You're welcome.

